+# Deployed-bytecode claim map: Robinhood Chain Stock token
+
+## 5.10 Robinhood Chain Stock token: role guards on the deployed runtime
+
+The implementation behind every Robinhood Chain stock token (`Stock`, 0xb35490d6f9163DE4F80d88dc75c3516eb64C5aE2,
+chain 4663) is lifted from its deployed runtime (`scripts/lift/inputs/stock-runtime.hex`, registry row `stock`).
+Its privileged functions ask the access registry 0xe10b6f6b275de231345c20d14ab812db62151b00 by `STATICCALL`;
+the registry's code is never assumed.
+
+| Claim | Theorem | Level / kind | Premises | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| The certificate checks against the exact deployed runtime (11,614 bytes, sha256 0ac99e9c…deec2), jump destinations included | `Blanc.Lift.Stock.cert_check` (`Blanc/Lift/Stock/Check.lean:33`), `Blanc.Lift.Stock.jumps_ok` (`Blanc/Lift/Stock/Jumps.lean:10`) | Kernel decision | none | the producer is untrusted; acceptance is the kernel decision |
+| Every successful `pause()` asked the registry `hasRole(TOKEN_PAUSER_ROLE, caller)` over the frame's own starting world and was answered with at least 32 bytes whose first word is 1 | `Blanc.Lift.Stock.pause_requires_role` (`Blanc/Lift/Stock/Pause.lean:848`), with the role tied to its name by `Blanc.Lift.Stock.tokenPauserRole_eq_keccak` (`Blanc/Lift/Stock/Pause.lean:40`) | Frame / guard | CODE; covered fork; fresh frame at pc 0 (empty stack and memory); selector `0x8456cb59` | safety only: no claim that a call with the role succeeds; reading it about Robinhood Chain carries the premise that Arbitrum Nitro executes these instructions as Ethereum does; the beacon proxy's forwarding is not lifted |
